Notebook[{Cell["Band corepresentations with MSGCorep", "Title"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["MagneticTB help home", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MagneticTB/guide/MagneticTB"]}], "Text"], Cell["To identify the symmetry of a band at a high-symmetry k point, use its small corepresentation. For magnetic space group 164.87, the examples below compare spinor and scalar s bases at Gamma, K, and A.", "Text"], Cell["This calculation uses the external MSGCorep package and its SpaceGroupIrep dependency. Install both first, then load MSGCorep and MagneticTB in a fresh kernel as shown below. MSGCorep must be loaded by the user:", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["Needs[\"MSGCorep`\"];\nNeeds[\"MagneticTB`\"];"], "Input"], Cell["Use one ordered MSGCorep operation list", "Section"], Cell["Use getMSGElemFromMSGCorep to obtain the symmetry operations, and pass them to init without changing their order. The printed primitive vectors give the lattice for this example. The corepresentation calculation requires this operation list; do not replace it with a list from msgop.", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["corepOperations = getMSGElemFromMSGCorep[{164, 87}];"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData[InterpretationBox[RowBox[{"\"Primitive Lattice Vector: \"", "", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"0", ",", RowBox[{"-", "a"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{FractionBox[RowBox[{SqrtBox["3"], " ", "a"}], "2"], ",", FractionBox["a", "2"], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "c"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "Primitive Lattice Vector: "*{{0, -a, 0}, {(Sqrt[3]*a)/2, a/2, 0}, {0, 0, c}}, Editable -> False]], "Print"], Cell["Double-valued high-symmetry calculation", "Section"], Cell["Place {sup,sdn} at the origin to calculate double-valued corepresentations. Here we keep only the onsite term, with the same energy e1 for both states, to show how the result depends on the chosen basis.", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["init[\n  lattice -> {\n    {0, -a, 0},\n    {Sqrt[3] a/2, a/2, 0},\n    {0, 0, c}\n  },\n  lattpar -> {a -> 1, c -> 2},\n  wyckoffposition -> {{{0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0}}},\n  symminformation -> corepOperations,\n  basisFunctions -> {{\"sup\", \"sdn\"}}\n];\ncorepHamiltonian = symham[1];\ncorepHamiltonian // MatrixForm"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData[InterpretationBox[RowBox[{"\"Generators:\"", "", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"I\"", ",", "\"T\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"C3+\"", ",", "\"F\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"C21pp\"", ",", "\"T\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "Generators:"*{{"I", "T"}, {"C3+", "F"}, {"C21pp", "T"}}, Editable -> False]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[InterpretationBox[RowBox[{"\"params:\"", "", RowBox[{"{", "e1", "}"}]}], "params:"*{e1}, Editable -> False]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[RowBox[{"(", "⁠", GridBox[{{"e1", "0"}, {"0", "e1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1, RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "⁠", ")"}], Function[BoxForm`e$, MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output"], Cell["Specify Gamma, K, and A in reciprocal fractional coordinates and call getTBBandCorep. The function prints the k-point names and result tables. It returns Null, so no additional Out cell is expected:", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["getTBBandCorep[\n  {164, 87}, corepHamiltonian, {e1 -> 0},\n  {{0, 0, 0}, {1/3, 1/3, 0}, {0, 0, 1/2}}\n]"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData["k-name: Γ, k-point: {0, 0, 0}, little co-group: D3d"], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"bands\"", "\"energy\"", "\"degeneracy\"", "\"small corep\""}, {TemplateBox[{"-", "\"-\"", "1", "2"}, "RowWithSeparators"], "0", "2", "\"(Γ)\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(Γ\\), \\(4\\)]\\)(2)\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Center, Left}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxDividers -> {"RowsIndexed" -> {2 -> Directive[Thickness[0.4], GrayLevel[0.5]]}}, GridBoxFrame -> {"ColumnsIndexed" -> {{{1, -1}, {1, -1}} -> Thickness[0.4]}}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {Default, 3, 1, 1}}], "Grid"]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData["k-name: K, k-point: {1/3, 1/3, 0}, little co-group: D3"], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"bands\"", "\"energy\"", "\"degeneracy\"", "\"small corep\""}, {TemplateBox[{"-", "\"-\"", "1", "2"}, "RowWithSeparators"], "0", "2", "\"(K)\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(K\\), \\(4\\)]\\)\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(K\\), \\(5\\)]\\)(2)\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Center, Left}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxDividers -> {"RowsIndexed" -> {2 -> Directive[Thickness[0.4], GrayLevel[0.5]]}}, GridBoxFrame -> {"ColumnsIndexed" -> {{{1, -1}, {1, -1}} -> Thickness[0.4]}}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {Default, 3, 1, 1}}], "Grid"]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData["k-name: A, k-point: {0, 0, 1/2}, little co-group: D3d"], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"bands\"", "\"energy\"", "\"degeneracy\"", "\"small corep\""}, {TemplateBox[{"-", "\"-\"", "1", "2"}, "RowWithSeparators"], "0", "2", "\"(A)\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(A\\), \\(4\\)]\\)(2)\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Center, Left}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxDividers -> {"RowsIndexed" -> {2 -> Directive[Thickness[0.4], GrayLevel[0.5]]}}, GridBoxFrame -> {"ColumnsIndexed" -> {{{1, -1}, {1, -1}} -> Thickness[0.4]}}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {Default, 3, 1, 1}}], "Grid"]], "Print"], Cell["The columns list band indices, energy, degeneracy, and the small corepresentation. With e1 = 0, the two bands have zero energy and are doubly degenerate at all three points. Their labels are Gamma_4(2), K_4 K_5(2), and A_4(2), respectively; each label belongs to its own k point.", "Text"], Cell["Single-valued basis", "Section"], Cell["Now replace {sup,sdn} by a scalar s orbital. Use the same ordered symmetry operations, run init again, and recalculate the Hamiltonian before finding its corepresentations:", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["init[\n  lattice -> {\n    {0, -a, 0},\n    {Sqrt[3] a/2, a/2, 0},\n    {0, 0, c}\n  },\n  lattpar -> {a -> 1, c -> 2},\n  wyckoffposition -> {{{0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0}}},\n  symminformation -> corepOperations,\n  basisFunctions -> {{\"s\"}}\n];\ncorepHamiltonian = symham[1];\ncorepHamiltonian // MatrixForm"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData[InterpretationBox[RowBox[{"\"Generators:\"", "", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"I\"", ",", "\"T\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"C3+\"", ",", "\"F\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"C21pp\"", ",", "\"T\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "Generators:"*{{"I", "T"}, {"C3+", "F"}, {"C21pp", "T"}}, Editable -> False]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[InterpretationBox[RowBox[{"\"params:\"", "", RowBox[{"{", "e1", "}"}]}], "params:"*{e1}, Editable -> False]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[RowBox[{"(", "⁠", GridBox[{{"e1"}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1, RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "⁠", ")"}], Function[BoxForm`e$, MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output"], Cell[BoxData["getTBBandCorep[\n  {164, 87}, corepHamiltonian, {e1 -> 0},\n  {{0, 0, 0}, {1/3, 1/3, 0}, {0, 0, 1/2}}\n]"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData["k-name: Γ, k-point: {0, 0, 0}, little co-group: D3d"], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"bands\"", "\"energy\"", "\"degeneracy\"", "\"small corep\""}, {"1", "0", "1", "\"(Γ)\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(Γ\\), \\(1\\)]\\)(1)\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Center, Left}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxDividers -> {"RowsIndexed" -> {2 -> Directive[Thickness[0.4], GrayLevel[0.5]]}}, GridBoxFrame -> {"ColumnsIndexed" -> {{{1, -1}, {1, -1}} -> Thickness[0.4]}}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {Default, 3, 1, 1}}], "Grid"]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData["k-name: K, k-point: {1/3, 1/3, 0}, little co-group: D3"], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"bands\"", "\"energy\"", "\"degeneracy\"", "\"small corep\""}, {"1", "0", "1", "\"(K)\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(K\\), \\(1\\)]\\)(1)\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Center, Left}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxDividers -> {"RowsIndexed" -> {2 -> Directive[Thickness[0.4], GrayLevel[0.5]]}}, GridBoxFrame -> {"ColumnsIndexed" -> {{{1, -1}, {1, -1}} -> Thickness[0.4]}}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {Default, 3, 1, 1}}], "Grid"]], "Print"], Cell[BoxData["k-name: A, k-point: {0, 0, 1/2}, little co-group: D3d"], "Print"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"bands\"", "\"energy\"", "\"degeneracy\"", "\"small corep\""}, {"1", "0", "1", "\"(A)\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(A\\), \\(1\\)]\\)(1)\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Center, Left}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxDividers -> {"RowsIndexed" -> {2 -> Directive[Thickness[0.4], GrayLevel[0.5]]}}, GridBoxFrame -> {"ColumnsIndexed" -> {{{1, -1}, {1, -1}} -> Thickness[0.4]}}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {Default, 3, 1, 1}}], "Grid"]], "Print"], Cell["There is now one nondegenerate band, with labels Gamma_1(1), K_1(1), and A_1(1). Both examples use zero onsite energy, but the spinor and scalar bases give double-valued and single-valued corepresentations, respectively.", "Text"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["History", "HistorySection"], Cell[TextData[{"New in: ", Cell["2.0.0", "HistoryData", CellTags -> "New"], " | Modified in: ", Cell[" ", "HistoryData", CellTags -> "Modified"], " | Obsolete in: ", Cell[" ", "HistoryData", CellTags -> "Obsolete"]}], "History"]}, Closed]], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Categorization", "CategorizationSection"], Cell["Tech Note", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Entity Type"], Cell["MagneticTB", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Paclet Name"], Cell["MagneticTB`", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Context"], Cell["MagneticTB/tutorial/Corepresentations", "Categoriza